<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kahk-tiliw-chan-chaak"><span class="enc-name">K'ahk' Tiliw Chan Chaak</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'ahk' Tiliw Chan Chaak was a king of the Classic Maya city of Naranjo, enthroned in 693 as a child, with his mother Lady Six Sky of Dos Pilas acting as ruler.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kak-tiliw-chan-yopaat"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kak-tiliw-chan-yopaat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat was the ruler of the Maya city of Quiriguá, installed in 724 under the authority of Copán.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kakupakal"><span class="enc-name">K'ak'upakal</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'ak'upakal, &quot;Fire Shield&quot;, was a lord of Chichen Itza in the second half of the 9th century and the figure most often named in the city's hieroglyphic inscriptions…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kan-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kan-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">K'an II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'an II was king of the Maya city of Caracol in Belize from 618 to 658.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kan-joy-chitam-ii"><span class="enc-name">K'an Joy Chitam II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'an Joy Chitam II was king of the Maya city of Palenque from 702, a son of K'inich Janaab' Pakal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kawiil-chan-kinich"><span class="enc-name">K'awiil Chan K'inich</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'awiil Chan K'inich was the fourth ruler of the Classic Maya kingdom of Dos Pilas in Guatemala, reigning from 741.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kiche-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kiche-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">K'iche' people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The K'iche' are a Maya people of the western highlands of Guatemala, centred on the departments of El Quiché, Totonicapán and Quetzaltenango.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-baaknal-chaak"><span class="enc-name">K'inich B'aaknal Chaak</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich B'aaknal Chaak was the ruler of the Maya city of Toniná, in Chiapas, Mexico, from 688 into the early 8th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-bahlam-ii"><span class="enc-name">K'inich B'ahlam II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich B'ahlam II was a Classic Maya king of Waka', the city now called El Perú, in the north-western Petén of Guatemala, in the late 7th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-janaab-pakal"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kinich-janaab-pakal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">K'inich Janaab Pakal</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich Janaab Pakal was king of Palenque from 615 to 683, the most celebrated ruler of the Classic Maya.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-kan-bahlam-ii"><span class="enc-name">K'inich Kan B'ahlam II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich Kan B'ahlam II was king of Palenque from 684 to 702, succeeding his father K'inich Janaab Pakal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-tatbu-skull-iv"><span class="enc-name">K'inich Tatbu Skull IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich Tatbu Skull IV was the last known king of the Maya city of Yaxchilan, recorded on Lintel 10 around 808.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-yat-ahk-ii"><span class="enc-name">K'inich Yat Ahk II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich Yat Ahk II was the last known king of the Classic Maya city of Piedras Negras on the Usumacinta river, ruling from 781.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-yax-kuk-mo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kinich-yax-kuk-mo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo'</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo' was the founder of the royal dynasty of Copán, in present-day Honduras, who took power in 426 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kiqab"><span class="enc-name">K'iq'ab</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'iq'ab was a K'iche' Maya king of the mid-15th century, under whom the kingdom ruled from Q'umarkaj reached its greatest extent across western Guatemala and the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kuk-bahlam-i"><span class="enc-name">K'uk' B'ahlam I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K'uk' B'ahlam I was the founder of the royal dynasty of Palenque, the Maya city in Chiapas, Mexico.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/k-j-stahlberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/k-j-stahlberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">K. J. Ståhlberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kaarlo Juho Ståhlberg was a Finnish lawyer and the first president of the Republic of Finland, serving from 1919 to 1925.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/k-p-sharma-oli"><span class="enc-name">K. P. Sharma Oli</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">K.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kaba-ye-zartosht"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kaba-ye-zartosht.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ka'ba-ye Zartosht</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ka'ba-ye Zartosht is a square stone tower of the Achaemenid period at Naqsh-e Rostam near Persepolis in Iran; its original purpose is still debated.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kaaba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kaaba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kaaba</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kaaba is a cube-shaped building at the centre of the Great Mosque of Mecca, the holiest site in Islam.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kaabu-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kaabu Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kaabu Empire was a Mandinka state in present-day Guinea-Bissau, Senegal and The Gambia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabah"><span class="enc-name">Kabah</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kabah is a Maya archaeological site in the Puuc hills of Yucatán, Mexico, about 20 km south-east of Uxmal, to which it was linked by a raised causeway (sacbe) ending in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabaka-of-buganda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kabaka-of-buganda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span 