ass="enc-name">Kabasa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kabasa was the royal capital of the Kingdom of Ndongo in present-day Angola, on the plateau between the Lukala and Kwanza rivers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabayama-hisataka"><span class="enc-name">Kabayama Hisataka</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kabayama Hisataka was a samurai of the Shimazu clan of Satsuma who commanded the invasion of the Ryukyu Kingdom in 1609.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabirdham-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kabirdham-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kabirdham district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kabirdham district is a district of Chhattisgarh, India, with its headquarters at Kawardha.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabompo-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kabompo-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kabompo River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kabompo is a river of north-western Zambia, a major tributary of the upper Zambezi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabongo-luba"><span class="enc-name">Kabongo Luba</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Kabongo Luba was one of the two states into which the Luba kingdom split after a succession civil war in the late nineteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kaboyo-olimi-i"><span class="enc-name">Kaboyo Olimi I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kaboyo Olimi I was the founder of the Kingdom of Toro in western Uganda.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kabuki"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclope